{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>A silver basin.</b> The numerical value of its letters by gematria is 930 — corresponding to the years of the first man." "<b>One hundred and thirty shekels its weight.</b> After the name of — when he stood up to beget children for the survival of the world, he was 130 years old, as it says ״וַיְחִי אָדָם שְׁלֹשִׁים וּמְאַת שָׁנָה וַיּוֹלֶד״ and so forth (Genesis 5)." "<b>One silver bowl.</b> By gematria 520 — after the name of Noah, who stood up to beget children at 500 years, and after the name of the twenty years that the decree of the Flood was decreed before his begetting of children — as I explained at ״וְהָיוּ יָמָיו מֵאָה וְעֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה״ (ibid. 6). Therefore it says מִזְרָק אֶחָד כֶסֶף — and it does not say מִזְרָק כֶסֶף אֶחָד as it says regarding the basin — to tell that even the letters of אֶחָד join the count." "<b>Seventy shekels.</b> Corresponding to the seventy nations that came forth from his sons."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:51.880667832Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}